description: Next.js server-domain patterns (no NestJS)
globs: apps/web/src/server/**/*.ts,apps/web/src/app/api/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# Server (`apps/web/src/server`)

- One folder per domain; **business logic in services**, not in route handlers/resolvers.
- Validate all inputs with Zod. RBAC on every sensitive mutation.
- Cart totals, coupons, inventory, compatibility, payment confirmation = **server only**.
- Stripe: verify webhook signatures; never mark paid from client redirect alone.
- Abandoned carts: PostgreSQL + cron Route Handler (`/api/cron/...`) or Vercel Cron — **no** Redis/BullMQ/Nest schedule.
- Email + R2: dedicated server modules; never expose secrets to the browser.
- Structured logging; GraphQL errors use stable codes — no stack/DB leaks to clients.
